<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Small World Media handles information collected through smallworld.media and its private QuickBooks integration."
  updated="October 13, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Small World Media LLC (“Small World Media”, “we”, “us”) is a creative studio in San Diego, California.
    This policy explains what information we collect through this website, smallworld.media, and through
    SWM Bookkeeping, a private QuickBooks Online integration we use for our own books, and how we use it.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>We don’t use analytics, advertising trackers or cookies on this site.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form.</strong> When you send an inquiry, we receive the name, email address, project
      details and message you enter. Our host, Netlify, processes the form and delivers it to us by email. We use it
      only to reply to you and to discuss the project you asked about.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting and delivery.</strong> Like any website, the services that deliver these pages receive
      your IP address and basic request details (browser, time, page requested). These are Netlify (hosting),
      Google Fonts (typefaces) and jsDelivr (a script for the animated background). Their own privacy policies
      govern that data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>SWM Bookkeeping (QuickBooks integration)</h2>
  <p>
    SWM Bookkeeping is an internal tool. It connects only to Small World Media’s own QuickBooks Online company,
    and it isn’t offered to, or used with, any other business or QuickBooks user.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What it accesses.</strong> Through Intuit’s Accounting API, it reads and writes our company’s
      accounting records: the chart of accounts, transactions, vendors, journal entries and company details. It
      doesn’t use Intuit’s Payments or Payroll APIs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How it’s used.</strong> Only for our own bookkeeping: reconciling our accounts with bank and card
      statements, and recording entries the company owner has reviewed and approved.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>AI assistance.</strong> The owner uses an AI assistant, Anthropic’s Claude, to help prepare and
      apply those entries. Data the assistant reads from QuickBooks is processed by Anthropic to provide that
      service. We don’t allow it to be used to train AI models.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Storage and security.</strong> QuickBooks access tokens are stored encrypted in the macOS Keychain
      on the owner’s computer and are never shared. Working copies of reports and a log of every change are kept
      on the owner’s devices and in our private cloud storage. All connections to Intuit use HTTPS.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No selling or sharing.</strong> We don’t sell, rent or share QuickBooks data with anyone, apart from
      the AI assistant described above and our accountant or tax preparer when needed for our own filings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Disconnecting.</strong> Access can be revoked at any time from QuickBooks (Apps → My apps), which
      immediately stops the integration from reaching the company’s data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep contact-form messages for as long as we need them to work with you, and accounting records for as long
    as tax and business record-keeping rules require.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what information we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it, by emailing
    <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. California residents have these rights under the CCPA. We don’t sell or
    share personal information as those terms are defined there.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site isn’t directed to children under 13, and we don’t knowingly collect their information.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we’ll update it here and change the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Small World Media LLC · San Diego, California ·
    <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
